      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The narrative of \"taking back control\" is intellectually dishonest because it falsely frames international cooperation as a form of external control rather than a necessary framework for modern stability. Real sovereignty in the 21st century requires participation in global institutions to manage transnational threats like climate change, pandemics, and financial instability. By advocating for isolation, nationalists aren't regaining control; they are voluntarily forfeiting the collective security and economic advantages that global engagement provides. Their \"sovereignty\" is merely a euphemism for self-imposed vulnerability.",
      "source": "target",
